Given an array of integers, count the number of unique pairs of
integers that have difference k.
Input: [1, 7, 5, 9, 2, 12, 3] K=2
Output: 4
We have four pairs with difference 2: (1, 3), (3, 5), (5, 7), (7, 9). Note
that we only want the number of these pairs, not the pairs themselves.


SOLUTION
we generate HashMap based on k
(key,key+k)
then we check if value exist on HashMap as key or not!
I AM REALLY SMART!



Note: if we want to do this logic by array
      we need nested loop (O(n^2))
                                 (on each element we need traverse the list to check
                                  if there is key+k or not)
      but we solve it by O(n)